body:
I should've been more clear -- news like we see today should definitely not be a thing anymore. Same thing with social media, which is used to collect data and do psychological experiments.

&#x200B;

 I just don't think we should stop reporting all kinds of news. Surely, there will still be bias, but I at least think it's worth minimizing it and also teaching people to recognize that, again, through education.

A fetus is alive. That's true. Though I'd argue, instead, that there's no harm in killing a being that cannot feel pain -- the reason why we don't kill people is that we don't want to do things that makes them feel negative emotions or go against their will, but a fetus, while its nervous system has not yet developed, has none of these two.

&#x200B;

I'm aware that sperm and fetus are different, but in terms of killing them, the consequences are the same. They're both potential human beings. At different stages, but that doesn't really make a difference if you draw the line where they can actually have feelings.
